content:
The orders exist and have statuses like "invoiced" and "paid" — not "confirmed". No webhook errors. This suggests the order-service is failing to transition orders to "confirmed" status, or payment-service is writing "captured" but the confirmation step that sets order status to "confirmed" is broken in a way that doesn't log errors. Let me check the order status transition and whether payment-service is calling the right confirmation path.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT o.status, COUNT(*) as cnt, MIN(o.updated_at) as first_seen FROM orders o WHERE o.updated_at >= 489 GROUP BY o.status ORDER BY first_seen",
      "why": "Check whether orders stopped reaching 'confirmed' status after the deploy at t=489, and what statuses they are stuck in instead"
    },
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT o.status, COUNT(*) as cnt FROM orders o WHERE o.updated_at < 489 GROUP BY o.status",
      "why": "Baseline order status distribution before the deploy, to compare with post-deploy distribution and confirm the regression"
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "payment-service",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "The v1.1 deploy at t=489 refactored webhook error handling and silently broke the step that transitions orders from 'paid'/'invoiced' to 'confirmed' after payment capture, leaving orders stuck in intermediate states without logging errors.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E3", "E9"],
      "refuting": ["E10"],
      "explains": ["I1_payment_has_order"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {"action": "rollback_service", "params": {"service": "payment-service"}},
        {"action": "replay_payment_confirmations", "params": {}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "payment-service v1.1 deploy at t=489 silently broke order confirmation after capture; orders are stuck in 'paid'/'invoiced' instead of 'confirmed', with no webhook errors logged."
}
```
